## Operational Insights

### Golden Signals Monitoring

The dashboards focus on the four "golden signals" of observability:

1. **Latency:** Request processing time (visible in Nginx logs, future Loki integration)
2. **Traffic:** System load, network bytes/sec (gauges and timeseries)
3. **Errors:** Alert firing frequency, error rates (alert rules configured)
4. **Saturation:** CPU%, Memory%, Disk% (gauges with thresholds)

### Alert Thresholds

Alert rules are configured for production readiness:

| Alert | Threshold | Duration | Action |
|-------|-----------|----------|--------|
| HighCPU | >80% | 5 min | Warning |
| CriticalCPU | >95% | 2 min | Critical |
| LowMemory | <20% free | 5 min | Warning |
| CriticalMemory | <10% free | 2 min | Critical |
| LowDiskSpace | <15% free | 5 min | Warning |
| CriticalDiskSpace | <5% free | 2 min | Critical |

These rules help predict problems before they occur.

