## Metrics & Measurements

### What This Enables

**Before Phase 4:** No visibility into system behavior  
- Problems only discovered when users complain
- No historical data to correlate with incidents
- Impossible to predict capacity issues

**After Phase 4:** Complete system visibility  
- See problems in real-time (CPU spike, memory leak)
- 15+ days of historical data to investigate
- Capacity predictions from trend analysis
- Alert triggers for proactive response

### Real-World Example

A typical production incident before and after Phase 4:

**Without monitoring:**
- 3:00 PM: User reports slow website
- 3:15 PM: You SSH in, vaguely check system
- 3:30 PM: Restart services (no idea what caused it)
- 4:00 PM: Problem recurs, repeat above
- User satisfaction: Frustrated

**With Phase 4:**
- 2:58 PM: Prometheus alert fires (CPU >80% for 5 min)
- 3:00 PM: You're alerted before users notice
- 3:05 PM: Check Grafana dashboard, see CPU spike correlated with specific time
- 3:10 PM: Check Prometheus metrics, identify the culprit process
- 3:15 PM: Fix applied with root cause understood
- User satisfaction: Unaware there was an issue

